  "metaDescription": "Indonesian National Police Chief General Suyudi Ario Seto has transferred Ahrie Sonta and Eko Hadi following a case involving the illegal wiretapping.",
  "aiSummaryBullets": [
    "Police Chief General Suyudi Ario Seto transferred several high-ranking officers involved in an illegal wiretapping case.",
    "Inspector General Ahrie Sonta and Inspector General Eko Hadi were moved to Yanma Polri following their involvement in the scandal.",
    "Investigations continue into the broader case involving allegations of treason and the potential involvement of other senior officers."
  ],
  "aiContextParagraph": "The Indonesian National Police (Polri) has initiated a series of leadership rotations and personnel movements involving high-ranking officers implicated in a wiretapping investigation. Inspector General Ahrie Sonta and Inspector General Eko Hadi were recently reassigned to the Yanma Polri unit after being associated with the unauthorized surveillance of President Prabowo Subianto. These transfers follow earlier disciplinary actions where Eko Hadi was dismissed from the force. While Ahrie Sonta and Eko Hadi remain central figures in the ongoing administrative and criminal inquiries, legal proceedings regarding the potential involvement of other senior figures, such as Inspector General Slamet Uliandi, are reportedly still under consideration. Authorities from the Witness and Victim Protection Agency (LPSK) continue to review protection requests as Bareskrim Polri investigates possible connections between the surveillance activity and broader allegations of treason against the state.",
